        "original_id": "0a248498-4efc-541c-a523-62acd979a528",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Williams Gunnison\n- Places: Mount Gunnison, Tomichi Dome, Mount Crested Butte, Gothic Mountain, Whetstone Mountain, Mount Axtel, Anthracite Range, Round Mountain, Carbon Peak, Beckwith Mountain, Marcellina Mountain\n- Concepts: laccoliths, Gunnison Country\n\nFacts:\n- John Williams Gunnison was born on November 11, 1812, and died on October 26, 1853.\n- John Williams Gunnison was an American military officer and explorer.\n- Mount Gunnison is named in honor of John Williams Gunnison, who explored the area.\n- Tomichi Dome and Mount Gunnison are among the laccoliths of the Gunnison Country.\n- Mount Crested Butte, Gothic Mountain, Whetstone Mountain, Mount Axtel, Anthracite Range, Round Mountain, Carbon Peak, Beckwith Mountain, and Marcellina Mountain are also laccoliths of the Gunnison Country.",
